===== 5. The gate, before the fix =====
# this is what the pipeline saw on the first run: fastapi 0.115.6 pulled
# starlette 0.41.3, which carries three HIGH findings

$ cat ../13_Final_Project_TaskBoard/backend/.trivyignore | head -22
# Accepted risks, reviewed 2026-10-07, to be re-checked 2027-01-07.
#
# Both are in starlette, which arrives as a dependency of fastapi rather than
# being chosen here. Upgrading does not resolve them: fastapi 0.142.2 is the
# newest release and it resolves starlette to 0.52.1, while the fixes landed in
# the starlette 1.x line. Pinning starlette==1.3.1 alongside fastapi gives
# ResolutionImpossible, so there is no version pair that satisfies both.
#
# CVE-2026-48818  SSRF and NTLM credential theft via UNC paths in StaticFiles.
#                 Not reachable here: this service mounts no StaticFiles, the
#                 frontend is served by a separate nginx container.
#
# CVE-2026-54283  request.form() limits ignored for urlencoded bodies, a DoS.
#                 Not reachable here: every endpoint takes JSON through
#                 pydantic models and none calls request.form().
#
# Revisit when fastapi supports the starlette 1.x line.
CVE-2026-48818
CVE-2026-54283

===== 6. The gate, after the fix =====
# fastapi bumped to 0.142.2, and the two unfixable findings accepted
# in writing. exit code 0 means the pipeline may continue.

$ docker run --rm -v /var/run/docker.sock:/var/run/docker.sock -v "$HOME/.cache/trivy:/root/.cache/trivy" -v "$PWD/../13_Final_Project_TaskBoard/backend/.trivyignore:/.trivyignore" aquasec/trivy:0.58.1 image --severity HIGH,CRITICAL --ignore-unfixed --ignorefile /.trivyignore --exit-code 1 --format table taskboard-backend:scan 2>/dev/null | tail -6; echo "gate exit code: $?"

taskboard-backend:scan (debian 13.7)
====================================
Total: 0 (HIGH: 0, CRITICAL: 0)

gate exit code: 0

